      "writtenOn": "2025-08-18T14:59:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do we actually need the memory barriers here? \n\nI mimicked the `mod_handlers` logic. However you\u0027re right, we don\u0027t expect the module to register the ops after the modules are initialized, if the module does so it is just a bad implementation. \n\nMaybe `__ro_after_init` would make more sense here?",
      "parentUuid": "282a0a9a_f3f39b57",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 246,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 246,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "0a1b3d57002db824f9a57df6711882975c91987f",
